WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.868
-Thank you very much, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.637
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.773
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.107
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.509
We have a great show
for you tonight.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.812
Bruce Springsteen
is here in studio.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.814
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.249
I saw Bruce backstage.
I said,

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:18.984
"Thank you so much for being
here on the first night

00:00:18.984 --> 00:00:20.686
of Hanukkah."
And Bruce said,

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:23.423
[ As Springsteen ] "Jimmy, for
the last time, I'm not Jewish."

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:28.427
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.096
[ Normal voice ]
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.898
Well, guys, things aren't
going too well

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.366
for President Trump lately,
but that didn't stop him

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.437
from throwing a party
last night. Watch this.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.239 line:0%
-Overnight, President Trump
hosting a Hanukkah party

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:43.576 line:0%
at the White House using the
holiday gathering to once again

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.479 line:0%
falsely claim
he can still win the election.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.588
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.224
Ah, yes, the festival of lies.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.693
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.294
Even the dreidel was looking at
Trump like,

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:03.997
"Damn, this guy spins
more than I do."

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.831
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.833
I like how everyone whipped out
their phones

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.002
to record Trump
like it was a drunken fight

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:11.504
in a Waffle House. Like,

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:15.608
"Oh, this is going to go viral.
This is going to get some hits."

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.509
It's probably good that Trump
talked about the election.

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:19.746
I feel like him winging
the story of Hanukkah

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.913
might have been worse.
It's like,

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:22.548
[ As Trump ] "For eight nights,

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:25.852
Jewish Santa would visit
all the good little Kushners."

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.987
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.222
[ Normal voice ]
Speaking of the White House,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.923
I read that once Trump
moves out,

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.859
officials are going to disinfect
the whole building

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:36.329
before Biden moves in.
-Yes!

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:40.165
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:41.834
I have a feeling this is going
to be necessary

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.570
with or without COVID.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.441
There's a half-eaten Baconator
between the cushions here.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.510
"Turn on the black light.
Good God! Oh, my --"

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.646
-Eww!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:57.783
-"My retinas are burning!
Oh, my --"

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:00.019
Biden's going to be the first
president to be sworn in,

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:03.623
then spend the next week
crashing at a La Quinta.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.426
Apparently, the CDC told Biden
it would be safer

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.928
if he just moved
into a bowling shoe.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.297
That doesn't sound -- That
doesn't sound right, does it?

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.266
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.602
Speaking of Biden,
I heard that he might take

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.870
an Amtrak train
to his inauguration,

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.606
which is slightly different than
what other presidents have done.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:22.575
That brings us to our new
educational segment called

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:28.414
"Presidential Inaugurations:
Betcha Didn't Know!"

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:31.417
-Joe Biden might travel
to his inauguration by Amtrak,

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.186
but betcha didn't know
Jimmy Carter

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.420
traveled to his inauguration

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.155
by shooting himself
out of a cannon.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:39.692 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.827 line:0%
This has been
"Presidential Inaugurations:

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.796 line:0%
Betcha Didn't Know!"
-Yeah, it's amazing.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.499 line:0%
I didn't know any of that.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.634
Listen to this --
a pharmaceutical company

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:52.771
had to issue a recall after
two of their drugs got mixed up.

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.674
Let's see which ones they were.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.509
-There is a recall this morning
after a drug

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.178 line:0%
used to treat depression
somehow got bottled up

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:02.148 line:0%
and sent out
with the generic form of Viagra!

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:07.119 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.655
-People knew something was up
when, well...

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.791
-Hey!
-...something was up.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.826
All right? Ah, come on.
[ Cymbals playing ]

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.727
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.727 --> 00:03:18.164
Yeah, the people in depression
commercials were like,

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.466
"Why do I have the sudden urge
to sit in an outdoor bathtub?"

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:24.536
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:29.208
Samsung just announced its new
110-inch microLED TV,

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:32.145
and it costs about $155,000.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:35.781
Yep, so now you have
a 110-inch TV playing

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:38.284
while you scroll through
Instagram on your phone.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.685
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.154
Can you lower that?

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.324
And finally, I saw that Jay-Z
just launched

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:48.027
his own premium brand of weed
called Monogram.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.962
It must be good.
Today, Jay-Z was like,

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.698
"I got two problems and forgot
the other 97!"

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.233
You know, some things happen
to you in life,

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.701
you just go, "Oh, my gosh,

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.035
I love that
that just happened

00:03:57.035 --> 00:03:59.004
because you just
made me so happy."

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:03.008
Well, last night, we just got
home from doing our show,

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:06.579
and everyone just started
sending me texts and they go,

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.015
"Dude, Dionne Warwick
just tweeted at you."

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.483
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.652
So Dionne Warwick is on Twitter
now, and she's like owning.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.421
She's running Twitter right now.
-Yes.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:18.458
-And it's so fun. And it's her.
And she tweeted,

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.159
"Does anybody know if
Jimmy Fallon will be doing

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.194
the Christmas Sweaters countdown
this year?

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:23.730
I love those wretched things."

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.465
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:28.067
Dionne Warwick.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.968
I flipped out,

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.738
and then I tweeted back to her,

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:34.673
and then she tweeted
back to me again.

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:35.975
-What?
-Yeah. And then I tweeted

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.710
back to her again.
And then I guess...

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.846
Did you send her a playlist?

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:42.081
-Oh, she got that?
-Dude, she got that and said,

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:47.653
"A playlist from Questlove
and a sweater from Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:50.122
I'm a happy lady, I can go to
bed happy" or something.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:52.258
I'm like,
"You are the greatest."

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.893
My dad...

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.428
I called my dad
after that happened

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:59.298
because she performed
on his aircraft carrier,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:03.102
the<i> USS Constellation</i>
in 1968 in San Diego.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.705
And trust me, I've heard
this story my whole life.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:08.540
And that's the whole story.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:12.345
But I think he saw her even
backstage and just said

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:13.679
how nice he was
and all this stuff.

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:15.882
So we've always been fans.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:18.184
And my dad said,
"I took a photo,"

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.620
and it's so great.
This is so my dad.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.888
So I go, "Yeah, you have a photo
of Dionne Warwick performing?"

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:24.190
And this is 1968.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.624
So it's one of those cameras

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:28.093
that have the cube flash,
the spinner.

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:31.497
So this is my dad's photo,
he says, of Dionne Warwick

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:35.034
performing on his...

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:37.070
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:44.109
That is his photo of
Dionne Warwick,

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:46.112
and it was cool.
I mean, I have photos like this,

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.780
too, at concerts where I'm like,
"Oh, my gosh,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.416
I'll never forget it."
But he really never forgot this

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.418
and talked about it
all the time.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.587
And so I thank Dionne
for just being awesome

00:05:55.587 --> 00:05:57.724
and all the jams.
She's unbelievable.

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.325
And I love you,
Dionne Warwick, so much.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:01.393
You just made my whole night
and world last night.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:03.228
So thank you for bringing up
the sweater.

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:06.532
We whipped up a special sweater
just for you, pal.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:09.668
One of these wretched sweaters.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:13.105
Check your mailbox 'cause this
guy's coming.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:14.173
Oh, look at this.

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.342 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:19.645 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:22.448
Only you can rock this, Dionne.

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:25.384
Only you could rock
this sweater.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.686
You'll make it look good,
and we love you.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:30.322
And thanks for thinking about us
and tweeting about us.

00:06:30.322 --> 00:06:32.458
Be well, pal. I hope to see you
and talk to you soon.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:35.594
We have exactly seven shows left
before we go on Christmas break,

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:36.661
which means it's time
for that beloved

00:06:36.661 --> 00:06:37.863
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:40.332
It's time for 12 days
of Christmas sweaters!

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:41.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:43.902
♪ 12 days
of Christmas sweaters ♪

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:48.240
♪ Seven days left ♪

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.877
-That's right! Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:06:50.877 --> 00:06:52.578
will be giving
one lucky audience member

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.480
a sensational Christmas sweater

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.248
from the countdown
to Christmas cabinet.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:58.050
Since there are
seven shows left,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.819
let's open door number 7.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:04.824
[ Drum roll ]
Go for it.

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:06.425
All right. Let's look at it.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:08.093
Beautiful. Oh!

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:09.528
Wow!

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:10.930
That is...

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:15.668
That is something else.
That is something else.

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:18.837
Yeah, literally, I think
it might be something else.

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:21.474
All right. Let's see who's going
home with tonight's sweater.

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.942
Everyone look at
your seat number.

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.443
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:25.878
Quest, can I get a drum roll,
please?

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:26.746
-Yeah.
[ Drum roll ]

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:29.381
-It is number...

00:07:29.381 --> 00:07:31.483
364!

00:07:31.483 --> 00:07:35.621
♪♪

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.590
-Hey!

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.992
Oh, my goodness. Look at this.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:42.495
Congratulations, you've won
tonight's Christmas sweater.

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:44.830
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.500
-Jenny, and I'm from Jersey.
-Jenny from Jersey!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.171
Jenny, would you mind
trying that on for us right now?

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:53.805
Is that okay?
-It's my favorite color.

00:07:53.805 --> 00:07:54.941
It really -- Oh, my gosh.

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:56.108
You are going to love this.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.677
There's no right way
to put it on.

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.078
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:00.879
Yeah, your head can go in
that way.

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:02.281
It doesn't really --
They are sleeves.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.849
That works. Yes.
Oh, this is --

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:06.318
Already I can tell.
Jenny?

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:09.322
Yes, just stop there.
That's perfect.

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.090
Jenny, it's almost too --
Yeah, it's perfect!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.059
Look at how beautiful.
Yeah. Look. Lookit!

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:15.928
This is what I'm talking about.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.196
Yeah. Come on, now!

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:18.697
Jenny, look at that.

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:20.165
You should be our model
for all these.

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:22.034
Congratulations.
Thanks again to Jenny,

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.235
our lucky audience member.
Stick around.

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:26.038
We'll be right back
with Bruce Springsteen!

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.140
Talking about Jersey?
Come on!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.276 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:33.846 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:37.383 line:0%
♪♪

